      "id": "table-3",
      "standard": "new",
      "title": "Table 3 — Where the overhead comes from (each stage × N, share of the cell)",
      "caption": "Each stage is its contribution to the Table 2 overhead: its time per instance × N, so commitment + interaction + the six buckets + Other add up to the cell (Total). Commitment is the serving overhead; interaction is the network wait at the reference profile (rounds × 1 ms + bytes ÷ 100 Gb/s, plus verifier compute the prover waits on); the buckets and Other are the proving overhead. A fused stage prints once in its first column, `↞` in the others. Setup, one-time (keys, circuit setup: `fixed.setup_seconds`) is outside the cell: its seconds, and ×native amortized over the measured batch (setup × N ÷ the batch's instances). Seconds per instance are in the drill-down below.",
      "rowHeader": "Cell",
      "columns": [
        "Commitment",
        "Interaction",
        "Witness",
        "Encoding + witness commitment",
        "Arithmetic",
        "Lookup",
        "ZK additional",
        "Serialization",
        "Other",
        "Total (the cell)",
        "Setup, one-time (not in the total)"
      ],
